return {h=9,w=1020,cr=120,hc=15,bh=70,gr="medium-slow",eg={"mineral"},st={70,105,105,50,40,20},ab={{5,0},{133,0},{159,1}},genus={en="Ore Pokémon",es="Pokémon Mineral",pt="Pokémon Minério"},flavor={en={[17]="When it overflows with power, the orange crystal on its body glows. It looks for underground water in caves.",[18]="Because its energy was too great to be contained, the energy leaked and formed orange crystals.",[21]="When it is healthy, its core sticks out. Always facing the same way, it swiftly moves front to back and left to right.",[22]="When it is healthy, its core sticks out. Always facing the same way, it swiftly moves front to back and left to right.",[23]="Because its energy was too great to be contained, the energy leaked and formed orange crystals.",[24]="When it is healthy, its core sticks out. Always facing the same way, it swiftly moves front to back and left to right.",[25]="Because its energy was too great to be contained, the energy leaked and formed orange crystals.",[26]="When it is healthy, its core sticks out. Always facing the same way, it swiftly moves front to back and left to right.",[27]="Its orange crystal is a mass of energy. Just one crystal fragment would provide enough fuel for a hundred dump trucks.",[28]="It explores caves in search of underground water. It’s not comfortable around water, so this Pokémon takes great care in lapping it up.",[29]="The energy overflowing from its body has turned into orange crystals that are hard enough to smash diamonds.",[30]="Its orange crystals are lumps of powerful energy. They’re valuable, so Boldore is sometimes targeted for them.",[33]="If you see its orange crystals start to glow, be wary. It’s about to fire off bursts of energy.",[34]="It relies on sound in order to monitor what’s in its vicinity. When angered, it will attack without ever changing the direction it’s facing."},es={[23]="La energía que no puede contener en el interior de su cuerpo se escapa formando cristales naranjas.",[24]